A||||5||Mark||Are Dunlop D60A2 discontinued?||||1||
Z||000000||Mark||07-05-2001||04:22 PM||||I've been looking to buy some Dunlop D60A2s when I came upon a "Clearance on all Dunlop D60A2" ad from NTB.  I called them, but they didn't have any 215/60-15's.  If they had them, they would have been $79 each -- some clearance, huh?<P>Tires.com still lists these tires for $56 each, but tirerack.com does not list them anymore.  Anyone know if these are being phased out?||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||07-05-2001||04:26 PM||||I don't know if they are being phased out or not, but I have seen these tires for sale recently at Peerless Tyre and Tires Plus, so they're still available for now.<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DavidHenshaw||07-05-2001||09:40 PM||||I just (2 mos ago) put these on front and rear of my car. Mine were shipped out of Charlotte, NC. Not aware of any discontinue.<P>Dave<P>86 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||WMEBERT||07-05-2001||10:14 PM||||I just bought a set of 215/60-15's for my '86 GT from Sears 3 weeks ago.  Their "$ale" price was $79.00 each which somehow ended up being $199.50 for the 2 and I didn't even get a road hazard warranty or pay their tire disposal fee because I kept the old tires.  NTB didn't have them.  I'd look around or try tirerack or someone else.<P>Good Luck <P>Bill <BR>86 GT||||reg||6
Z||000004||Two88GTs||07-06-2001||01:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mark:<BR><B>I've been looking to buy some Dunlop D60A2s when I came upon a "Clearance on all Dunlop D60A2" ad from NTB.  I called them, but they didn't have any 215/60-15's.  If they had them, they would have been $79 each -- some clearance, huh?<P>Tires.com still lists these tires for $56 each, but tirerack.com does not list them anymore.  Anyone know if these are being phased out?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think you're referring to D60A2 JLBs, the original D60A2s have been discontinued for a while now, methinks.  I had a set of JLBs installed on my 67k car 15k ago and now the rears are worn to almost nothing while the fronts still have good tread.  Sort of disappointed with the tread life but I guess my [lead] right foot has to share some of the blame.<P>A comparable tire is the BF Goodrich Comp T/A HR-4s that are maybe $2-3 more each depending on width, plus now you can take advantage of their "Buy 4 and get a GTech-Pro free" offer. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||BV MotorSports||07-06-2001||11:30 AM||||Its true the D60A2 has been discontinued, because it was replaced with the D60A2 JBL.<BR>I have always had the D60A2 JLB's on my car. I love em. AA traction rating, A temp rating and a 320 treadwear. They are H rated so good for up to 130mph<P>tirerack cost (my jobber cost)<P>205/60R 15 $49<BR>215/60R 15 $51<BR>225/60R 15 $54<P>On my Conquest's and Starions I run Kumho.<P>They dont offer a 60 series tire in the <BR>ECSTA Supra 712 but a 55 is close enuff. Kuhmo ECSTA Supra 712 directional speed rated hi performance tires. You'll love em !<BR>Up to ZR rated.<P>205/55VR 15 $59<P>All the sizes they have listed right now but more will come.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
